{"type":"route","meta":{"status":200,"headers":{"content-type":"application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/rss.xml/layout,_N_T_/rss.xml/route,_N_T_/rss.xml"}},"body":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:content=\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\"><channel><title>Virga</title><link>https://virga.site</link><description>Virga is a Cloudflare-only baseline for launch directories, newsletters and portfolios — one owner, many readers, no console.</description><atom:link href=\"https://virga.site/rss.xml\" rel=\"self\" type=\"application/rss+xml\"/><item><title>Shipping a launch directory on Cloudflare alone</title><link>https://virga.site/posts/shipping-a-directory</link><guid>https://virga.site/posts/shipping-a-directory</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>Upvotes, view counts and rankings without a database you have to run.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A launch directory needs exactly three things a static site cannot do:\ncount a view, take an upvote, and rank the list. Virga does all three in\none public Worker over D1, keyed on a daily visitor fingerprint that never\nidentifies a person.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-ts\">// one upvote per visitor per slug, per day\nPOST /v1/reactions/launches/acme { &quot;kind&quot;: &quot;upvote&quot; }\n</code></pre>\n<p>The ranking reads two small totals tables and never scans reactions.</p>\n]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>Hello, world — why this site exists</title><link>https://virga.site/posts/hello-world</link><guid>https://virga.site/posts/hello-world</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>The first issue: what Virga is, and what you can expect in this inbox.</description><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Welcome. This is the first issue of a newsletter that ships from a git\nrepository: every issue is a Markdown file, every send is a CLI command,\nand the only thing running is a handful of Cloudflare Workers.</p>\n<h2>What to expect</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>One email when something ships. Nothing else.</li>\n<li>Every issue archived here, with a public view count.</li>\n<li>Unsubscribe in one click, no questions.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Content is the configuration. The site renders the sections its folders\nfill, so the same tree is a newsletter, a portfolio or a directory.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>See you in the next one.</p>\n]]></content:encoded></item></channel></rss>"}